// Copy this file to Config/Signing.xcconfig (ignored by git) and fill in your
// Apple Developer team ID. project.yml references Config/Signing.xcconfig for
// both configurations; xcodegen generates the project with or without it
// (options.disabledValidations: missingConfigFiles), and CI builds with
// CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO, so the file is only needed for device builds and
// for scripts/archive_and_export.sh.
//
// The team ID is the 10-character identifier shown under Membership details
// at developer.apple.com. It is NOT the 10-character ID that appears inside an
// "Apple Development: Name (XXXXXXXXXX)" certificate name; that is a
// certificate user ID and Xcode rejects it as a team.
//
// Never commit the filled-in copy. See APPLE_DEVELOPER_WARNING.md.

DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = YOUR_TEAM_ID
